346:In the largest pooled neuroimaging sample of individuals at CHR-P to date, we identi /uniFB01 ed an absence of signi /uniFB01 cantly greater regional heterogeneity compared with HC, despite an emerging trend towards greater fronto-temporal and hippocampal heterogeneity in CHR-P. These /uniFB01 ndings persist irrespective of longitudinal transition to psychosis. Subsequent application of a personalised PBSI score revealed signi /uniFB01 cantly greater divergence in global neuroanatomical pro /uniFB01 les in CHR-P, and further, a small subgroup (approximately 10%) of individuals at CHR-P who demonstrate markedly divergent neuroanatomical pro /uniFB01 les of SA, CT and SV respective to a normative pro /uniFB01 le. Further clinical investigation of this subgroup is required in light of the limited clinical variables currently available.
